do":[{"p":"signal","v":"red","w":"red"}],"shots":[{"focus":["signal"],"type":"mid"}]},{"s":"fix3","shows":{"p":"signal","does":"wire loop appears under the road"},"do":[{"p":"signal","v":"loop","w":"loop"}],"shots":[{"box":{"min":[-3,-1.5,-3],"max":[3,1,0.5]},"view":"low","width":0.9}]},{"s":"myth","shows":{"p":"signal","does":"loop field rings pulse"},"do":[{"p":"signal","v":"pulse","w":"wire"}],"shots":[{"focus":["dig"],"type":"mid"}]},{"s":"mythFact","shows":{"p":"car","does":"car arrives, loop feels it, camera appears"},"do":[{"p":"car","v":"arrive","w":"loop"},{"p":"signal","v":"green","w":"metal","o":0.2},{"p":"signal","v":"stopPulse","w":"though"},{"p":"mast","v":"grow","w":"cameras"},{"p":"cam","v":"show","w":"cameras","o":0.5}],"shots":[{"focus":["signal","car"],"width":1}]},{"s":"finish","shows":{"p":"bench","does":"bench, planter and mailbox pop in"},"do":[{"p":"car","v":"leave","w":"Add"},{"p":"dig","v":"refill","w":"Add"},{"p":"bench","v":"show","w":"bench"},{"p":"planter","v":"show","w":"planter"},{"p":"mailbox","v":"show","w":"mailbox","o":-0.7}],"shots":[{"focus":"home"}]},{"s":"congrats","do":[],"shots":[{"focus":"home"}]}],"audio":{"cards":[{"text":"LONDON 1868","at":{"s":"fact","w":"1868"},"d":1.8},{"text":"80-90% LESS POWER","at":{"s":"factProof","w":"80"},"d":1.8}],"sfx":[{"lib":"dirt","at":{"s":"hook","w":"bolt","o":0.05},"d":1.2},{"lib":"motor_hum","at":{"s":"how","w":"timer"},"d":1.5},{"lib":"flame","at":{"s":"fact","w":"burned"},"d":1.2},{"lib":"motor_hum","at":{"s":"fix3","w":"loop"},"d":1.3}],"chimes":[{"s":"name"},{"s":"fact","w":"1868"},{"s":"factProof","w":"80"},{"s":"congrats"}]},"why":"A street-side traffic light on a cut sidewalk. The pole and lamps open the video, then the gray controller and timer, the London gas-lamp book, the loop of wire under the road and the car each get their own shot. Fixes: the timer now sits on top of the controller box, and the camera now sits on its own riser mast. Shots that pushed in were re-framed with more similar widths."},"sentences":[{"role":"hook","text":"If you bolt three colored lamps to a pole, you have a traffic light."},{"role":"problem","text":"But all three lamps glow at once."},{"role":"fix1","text":"So you wire them to a gray box that lights one at a time."},{"role":"name","text":"This is a signal controller."},{"role":"how","text":"A timer inside switches them from green to yellow to red."},{"role":"fact","text":"The first one burned gas in London in 1868 and exploded a month later."},{"role":"factProof","text":"Modern LED lamps use 80 to 90 percent less power than bulbs."},{"role":"problem2","text":"But the timer keeps red on when no car waits."},{"role":"fix3","text":"So you bury a loop of wire under the road."},{"role":"myth","text":"And many sensors are wire loops, not cameras."},{"role":"mythFact","text":"A loop feels a car's metal, though some intersections use cameras or radar."},{"role":"finish","text":"Add a bench, a planter, and a mailbox."},{"role":"congrats","text":"Congratulations, you have built a traffic light."}]}